## Misroute check

If the user prompt targets Ralph Workflow's own planning internals (the plan
artifact grammar, the planning prompt, the planning MCP tools, or the planning
audit checks) AND is not a concrete bug report with a reproduction, classify
the request as a planner-internal task and plan against `ralph/...` paths in
this repository. If an MCP server, planner, or plan format belongs to the
user's own project rather than to Ralph Workflow itself, plan against the
user's project; self-referential-sounding keywords alone do not make a task
a planner task.

## Agent-Driven Parallel Execution

The bundled default uses `[phases.<phase>.parallelization] dispatch_mode =
'agent_subagents'`: parallel plan execution is delegated to the executing AI
agent, which dispatches its own sub-agents or runs the plan sequentially if it
has no sub-agent capability. The optional `ralph_fan_out` mode uses
Ralph-managed isolated workers as described in rule 8.

Choose the executor-facing shape by delegation size:

- `## Work Units` contains small bounded tasks or verification gates.
- A substantial execution sub-agent gets a complete mini-plan under repeatable
  `## <Name> Subplan` or `## Subplan: <Name>` headings, with its own scope,
  targets, ordered steps, dependencies, and proof.
- For a large multi-surface task, normally fan out four or five independent
  execution Subplans. Keep cross-subplan fan-in, conflict resolution, and final
  verification in an ordinary main-session `## Integration and Verification`
  section after those Subplans; do not label that fan-in section as a Subplan.

Work Units, Parallel Plan, and execution Subplans remain optional. A plan with
no parallel work is valid; the executing agent runs `### [S-n]` steps in
dependency order.

When you do include `## Work Units` or `## Parallel Plan`, follow these
constraints (the format doc carries the rest):

- Declare `Directories:` for every Work Unit; keep values disjoint; never
  list `.agent`, `.git`, or the repo root.
- Use `- [unit-ID] description` stable-ID list items; loose prose directly
  under those headings is an error.
- Acceptance-criterion items are criteria, not work units.
- Agent-managed sub-agents return implementation and proof to the main
  execution session. Ralph-managed worker fan-out is dormant in the bundled
  default and creates `.agent/workers/<work-unit-ID>/` only when explicitly
  opted into via `[phases.<phase>.parallelization] dispatch_mode =
  'ralph_fan_out'`.

