## Plan-artifact canonical contract

The plan is ONE markdown document. Full document grammar, step guidance,
acceptance-criteria linking, severity model, the `## Validation Overrides`
ledger, and `## Design` section conventions live in
`.agent/artifact-formats/plan.md`. The validator reports the exact field,
line, and rule for every error and warning; repair the named field rather
than guessing at another schema. Override any advisory finding by recording
a reason under `## Validation Overrides`; errors cannot be overridden and
will still block submission.

Your target is to submit a plan that planning analysis can approve on the first pass. For test-running steps, prefer `Type: verify` with a concrete `Verify:` command and a specific `Expect:` result; a specific `Location:` artifact is the non-command alternative. Project-specific `Type:` values are accepted and preserved verbatim, so do not relabel useful domain vocabulary merely to fit the recommended built-ins. Use `### [S-n] Title` step blocks (e.g. `### [S-1] Title`) for each ordered step.

